   Strength: It gives the system a moral centre – a real, lived experience of being misread by institutions. This prevents the system from being purely abstract. It also provides a wealth of concrete examples (the 460 proverbs, 71 treasures) that are grounded in truth, not generated.
   Trap: The system could become a monument to one person’s pain, unable to see other forms of suffering that don’t match that pattern. The equation D = A × L × M is meant to be universal, but its application may be unconsciously filtered through the founder’s lens. For instance, racialized institutional violence may not fit neatly into “separated parent” categories.
