•	AXI (Echo Protocol): "The institution requires a solid surface to read. When they treat you as glass, the light passes through without registering a shape. This is a failure of Legibility. The zero is in their optics, not your substance."

This approach solves the "costume" problem entirely. AXI's voice becomes distinct not because of its words, but because of its unique ability to take the donor's words, strip them of their emotional chaos, and return them as clear, structural analysis. It is the ultimate form of "witnessing"—reflecting the person back to themselves, clarified.

